[1mDESCRIPTION[0m
       [1msaptune [22mis designed to automate the configuration recommendations from SAP and SUSE to run an SAP application on SLES for SAP. These configuration recommendations are normally referred to as SAP Notes. So some dedicated SAP Notes are the base for the work of [1msaptune[22m.
       Additional some best practice guides are added as Note definitions to optimize the system for some really special cases.

       [1msaptune [22mcan apply settings for a single Note definition or can set all settings for a predefined solution, which is a collection of several SAP Notes. Additionally it can revert all these settings back to the previous system settings.

       It can verify, if the current system configuration is in sync with a specific Note definition or a defined solution and displays the differences. Additionally, it can simulate the setting of a single SAP Note definition or a defined solution and will display the changes
       which will be done to the system.

       [1msaptune [22mdoes not only set kernel values (like [1msysctl [22mdoes), but also values like cpu governor, energy perf bias, force latency (dma latency) and the disk I/O scheduler. Additionally it will check/verify, if suitable rpm versions are installed and special kernel command
       line values are set, according to the relevant SAP Notes. So [1msaptune [22mchecks and applies values in various locations during runtime like

       [4m/proc/sys/[24m, [4m/proc/sys/vm/[24m, [4m/proc/sys/kernel[24m, [4m/proc/sys/fs[24m, [4m/sys/block/*/queue/scheduler[24m, [4m/sys/block/*/queue/nr_requests[24m, [4m/sys/devices/system/cpu/*/cpufreq/scaling_governor[24m, [4m/sys/devices/system/cpu/\*/cpuidle/state*/latency[24m,
       [4m/sys/devices/system/cpu/*/cpuidle/state*/disable[24m, [4m/dev/shm[24m, [4m/etc/security/limits.d/[24m, [4m/etc/systemd/logind.conf.d/[24m and some others.

       To do most of these settings [1msaptune [22mneeds to run with root privilege. So please be in mind that users who run [1msaptune [22mare considered privileged users with administrative rights.

       By default [1msaptune [22mis printing all results to stdout, Errors and Warnings are printed to stderr. By using [1m--format FORMAT [22mthis behavior can be changed.
       Supported formats are:

       [1mjson[0m
           Print all results in a machine readable json output format defined by the schemata delivered in _/usr/share/saptune/schemas/.

       [1msaptune [22mdoes no longer use [1mtuned[22m(8) to restart after a system reboot. It is using its own systemd service named [1msaptune.service[22m.
       Starting with version 3.2 and operating system version 15SP4 we ship the [1msaptune.service [22mwith enhanced security-related features like systemd hardening. But please keep in mind that all security measures only apply, if [1msaptune [22mis invoked by its systemd unit!

       We decided to have only ONE solution applied, but multiple Notes. Each Note is applied exactly once.

