[1mNOTE ACTIONS[0m
       Note denotes either a SAP Note, a vendor specific tuning definition or SUSE recommendation article.

       ===

       [1mapply[0m
           Apply optimization settings specified in the Note. The Note will be automatically activated upon system boot if the saptune service is enabled. + If a Note definition contains a '[1m[reminder][22m' section, this section will be printed after the Note has applied
           successfully. It will be highlighted with red color. + A Note can only be applied once. + ATTENTION: Please be in mind: If a Note definition to be applied contains parameter settings which are likewise set before by an already applied Note these settings get be
           overwritten.
           The last comes, the last wins, it’s all about 'order'. + So be careful when applying Solutions or Notes or when reverting Notes, especially if these Notes are part of an already applied Solution. You can re-apply such a Note, but the order - and may be the resulting
           parameter settings - will be unlike before.
           Special attention is needed, if customer or vendor specific Notes from [4m/etc/saptune/extra[24m are used. + But saptune will detect such conflicting settings during [4msaptune[24m [4mnote[24m [4mverify[24m or [4msaptune[24m [4mverify[24m [4mapplied[24m and will print a footnote with a pointer to the 'winning'
           Note.
           This conflict detection will not work if the verify command is used on non-applied Notes.

       [1mlist[0m
           List all SAP Notes, vendor specific tuning definitions and SUSE recommendation articles that saptune is capable of implementing. + Currently implemented Notes are marked with '[1m+[22m', if manually enabled, '[1m*[22m', if enabled by Solutions or '[1m-[22m', if a Note belonging to an
           enabled Solution was reverted manually. In all cases the Notes are highlighted with green color.
           If an [1moverride [22mfile exists for a NoteID, the Note is marked with '[1mO[22m' and a customer or vendor specific Note is marked with '[1mC[22m'.
           If we detect a [1mconflict [22mwith Notes the related entry in the list is marked with a leading '[1m![22m' and the line is highlighted with yellow color. Look at the log file for details like warning messages addressing the problem.
           Currently we report a conflict if a customer or vendor specific Note has the [1msame [22mname as a shipped Note. In this case the shipped Note will take precedence over the custom Note.

       [1menabled[0m
