[1mHOTFIX[0m
       A HotFix is a new way to react fast to [1mcritical bugs[22m, that can harm SAP installations.
       It is meant to bridge the time with a [1mtemporary mitigation [22muntil the [1mpermanent fix [22mis available. As soon as the fix is released, the next released saptune version will contain an [1mupdate [22mto the HotFix to be applied only when necessary. [1mOne year [22mafter the fix is available,
       we will [1mremove [22mthe HotFix from saptune.

       We hope to provide an comfortable way to address such issues.

       The HotFix will be added as individual Note with the name
       [1mHotFix<TID_NUMBER> [22mand can be part of a Solution.
       A HotFix release will contain only configuration changes and no new features.

       To activate the HotFix you can simply apply the Note by

       [4msaptune[24m [4mnote[24m [4mapply[24m [4mHotFix<TID_NUMBER>[0m
       which will not interrupt your current tuning but add the needed parameter settings. The change will take effect immediately and is reboot persistent.

       Or you [4mrestart[24m [4mthe[24m [4msaptune.service[24m, which will lead to a short gap in your tuning because of the 'revert'/'apply' workflow of the service restart. Your SAP workload should be stopped for this operation.

       Or you reboot your server.

       As soon as the permanent fix is available and installed on the system, the Hotfix can be reverted with
       [4msaptune[24m [4mnote[24m [4mrevert[24m [4mHotFix<TID_NUMBER>[0m

       The next released saptune version will contain an update of the HotFix with a condition ([1mtag[22m) to apply this HotFix only under the condition the permanent fix is not installed on the systems.
       The HotFix will be removed from saptune one year after the permanent fix is available, giving customers enough time to update their systems.

